{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Many days.</b> More than those of Hebron. In Hebron he spent 25 years, and here 26 — for he was 75 years old when he left Haran; that same year ״וַיָּבֹא וַיֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵלֹנֵי מַמְרֵא״ — for we do not find that he settled anywhere before that; in all his other stations he was like a traveler who camps and moves on and goes, as it says ״וַיַּעֲבֹר אַבְרָם״, ״וַיַּעְתֵּק מִשָּׁם״, ״וַיְהִי רָעָב בָּאָרֶץ וַיֵּרֶד אַבְרָם מִצְרַיְמָה״ (Genesis 12), and in Egypt he spent only three months, for Pharaoh sent him away immediately; ״וַיֵּלֶךְ לְמַסָּעָיו״ until ״וַיָּבֹא וַיֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵלֹנֵי מַמְרֵא אֲשֶׁר בְּחֶבְרוֹן״ (ibid. 13) — there he stayed until Sodom was overturned; immediately ״וַיִּסַּע מִשָּׁם אַבְרָהָם״ — because of the shame of Lot — and came to the land of the Philistines, and he was 99 years old, for in the third year after his circumcision the angels came to him — that makes 25 years; and here it is written ״יָמִים רַבִּים״, more than the earlier ones. And Scripture does not come to obscure but to explain; and if they were more than those by two years or more, it would have specified them — so perforce they are not more than one year in excess; that makes 26 years. Immediately he left there and returned to Hebron, and that year preceded the binding of Isaac by 12 years, in Seder Olam."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:56.989239451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}